    "text": "To determine the total number of push-ups Bryan did, we need to break down the problem step by step.\n\n1. Calculate the number of push-ups in the first two sets:\n   - Each set consists of 15 push-ups.\n   - Bryan does 2 sets.\n   - Therefore, the number of push-ups in the first two sets is \\(15 \\times 2 = 30\\).\n\n2. Determine the number of push-ups in the third set:\n   - Bryan does 15 push-ups in the first two sets, so he has \\(15 - 5 = 10\\) push-ups left for the third set.\n   - Therefore, the number of push-ups in the third set is 10.\n\n3. Calculate the total number of push-ups:\n   - Add the number of push-ups from the first two sets to the number of push-ups from the third set.\n   - The total number of push-ups is \\(30 + 10 = 40\\).\n\nThus, the total number of push-ups Bryan did is \\(\\boxed{40}\\).",
